### 1. REGISTRATION - Create a new user (returns JWT token)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "sami@example.com",
  "firstName": "Sami",
  "lastName": "Ali",
  "password": "pass123",
  "active": true
}

###
### 2. REGISTRATION - Try to register with duplicate email (should fail)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "sami@example.com",
  "firstName": "Sami2",
  "lastName": "Ali2",
  "password": "pass123",
  "active": true
}

###
### 3. LOGIN - Login with registered email and password (returns JWT token)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "sami@example.com",
  "password": "pass123"
}

###
### 4. LOGIN - Try login with wrong password (should fail)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "sami@example.com",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

###
### 5. LOGIN - Try login with non-existent email (should fail)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nonexistent@example.com",
  "password": "pass123"
}

###
### 6. CREATE USER (direct user creation)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ashraf@example.com",
  "firstName": "Ashraf",
  "lastName": "Ali",
  "password": "secure123",
  "active": true
}

###
### 7. GET USER BY ID
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/users/3

###
### 8. UPDATE USER - Update all fields
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/users/4
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "mariam.updated@example.com",
  "firstName": "mariam",
  "lastName": "amen",
  "password": "newsecure456",
  "active": true
}

###
### 9. GET ALL USERS
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/users

###
### 10. DELETE USER
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/v1/users/4

